(Who am I without them? Who am I  [without]  Marvel and DC? Who am I without the  [people]  surrounding me? Who) Tj
T* (am I without these movies  [and]  series?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Beginning with a line from Dead Poets  [Society]  spoken by Robin Williams' character John Keating: “No  [matter] ) Tj
T* (what anyone tells you, words and ideas can  [change]  the world.”) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In the same way, the people  [you]  surround yourself with and the fictional characters you  [grow]  up with can also) Tj
T* (change you in beautiful  [ways] ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I'm not saying that the characters you see  [in]  shows and movies completely change you overnight after  [you]  start) Tj
T* (watching them. Rather, their influence gradually becomes  [a]  part of you over a period of time.  [They]  can amplify) Tj
T* (certain behaviours, introduce you to new  [ways]  of thinking, inspire you, and sometimes even encourage  [you]  to) Tj
T* (become a better person.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (When you try  [to]  explain this idea to someone around you —  [or]  perhaps even to yourself while reading this — ) Tj
T* ([they]  might think that you're borderline becoming insane. But  [maybe]  that simply means they haven't yet understood) Tj
T* (or  [noticed]  this phenomenon.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Be it learning to show empathy,  [like]  Barry Allen from The Flash, trying to put  [yourself]  in another person's shoes) Tj
T* (and see things from  [their]  point of view, standing alone and saying, “I  [can]  do this all day,” learning from our) Tj
T* (mistakes  [so]  that we don't repeat them, understanding the art  [of]  redemption, realizing that no amount of money can) Tj
T* ( [ever]  buy a second of time, redefining ourselves, or  [learning]  to pick ourselves up every time we fall  [—]  all of) Tj
T* (these ideas can contribute to our  [mentality]  in ways much larger than we initially expect.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* ( [And]  it isn't only about fictional characters. We learn  [countless]  things from the people around us and from  [the] ) Tj
T* (stories we experience. Some of them may be  [professional]  some personal, and some as simple as basic  [knowledge] ) Tj
T* (Yet, all of them contribute to our attitudes,  [behaviours]  and the way we see the world, often  [more]  than we realize.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (And who am I without  [some]  of the beautifully written quotes from movies and  [by]  some incredible writers?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (“Why do we fall, sir?  [So]  that we can learn to pick ourselves up.”  [-]  Alfred Pennyworth) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (“Annihilating is easy. Razing things to  [the]  ground is easy. Trying to fix what's broken  [is]  hard. Hope is hard.” -) Tj
T* (Loki) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (“You will  [have]  bad times, but they will always wake you  [up]  to the good stuff you weren’t paying attention  [to.”] ) Tj
T* (- Sean Maguire) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (“There is a natural order  [to]  things. Things happen the way they do. We  [may]  not know why at the time, but there ) Tj
T* ([must]  always be a reason.” - Henry Allen) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (“When  [a]  miracle is actually happening, nobody recognizes it... and  [once]  it has already happened, there is no need ) Tj
T* ([to]  recognize it.” - Trivikram Srinivas) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (“It’s not how  [well]  you play that matters, but when you stop.  [If]  you lose after winning, the loss will be ) Tj
T* ([remembered]  But if you win after losing, that victory  [will]  be remembered in history, because history only) Tj
T* (remembers  [how]  you finished.” - Venky Atluri) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (These are just  [a]  few quotes that popped into my mind while  [writing]  this post. There are countless other beautifully) Tj
T* (written  [lines]  that can change the way we perceive the  [world]  and even the way we perceive ourselves. ) Tj
T* (Many  [of]  my friends think that Marvel, DC, and movies  [are]  simply entertainment, and that these are nothing more ) Tj
T* ([than]  fictional characters. To them, it's just a movie  [or]  a franchise. To me, it's years of memories,  [excitement] ) Tj
T* (laughter, heartbreak, and the characters I grew up  [with]  Yes, they are fictional. But the impact they  [have]  left on) Tj
T* (some of our lives never was.) Tj
